WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:03.840
Shireen Baratheon: The Dance of Dragons.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.890
It's the story of the fight between Rhaenyra
Targaryen and her half-brother Aegon for control

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.230
of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:15.629
A True Telling by Grand Maester Munkun, being
a history of the war of Targaryen succession

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:21.810
between the Princess Rhaenyra and Aegon, Second
of his name, that nearly destroyed the realm.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:28.119
Viserys Targaryen: One night, a servant found
the old king had died in his sleep.

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:32.200
Protocol dictated that the bells would be
rung and a raven sent to Dragonstone to summon

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.960
the heir, Princess Rhaenyra, for her coronation.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.550
But Alicent had other plans.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.129
Ser Otto Hightower, the Hand of the King and
father to Queen Alicent, demanded that the

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:44.620
succession be settled immediately.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.980
The old king had forced the lords of Westeros
to swear fealty to Princess Rhaenyra as his

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:49.980
heir.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.950
But Ser Criston Cole rightly pointed out that
a son comes before a daughter.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:04.809
Shireen: Both of them thought they belonged
on the Iron Throne.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:08.790
When people started declaring for one of them
or the other, their fight divided the kingdoms

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:09.850
in two.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.900
Brothers fought brothers, dragons fought dragons.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.700
By the time it was over, thousands were dead.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:24.119
And it was a disaster for the Targaryens as
well.

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:29.390
They never truly recovered.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:35.659
Varys: During the great Targaryen civil war
known as "the Dance of the Dragons," a king

00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:41.909
and queen each vied for the throne, dividing
their house and its dragons against each other.

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:46.909
Eventually, the queen was fed to her rival's
dragons while her son watched, and the victorious

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:49.909
king soon died of his own wounds.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:55.790
By the war's end, King's Landing was smashed,
cities razed and sacked never to be rebuilt,

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:15.740
and dragons had faded from this world.

